================================================================
Getting speculation to actually run
================================================================
`-md <draft>` alone does NOT enable speculation in this version. It only sets the
draft model path. `common_params_speculative::types` defaults to
{COMMON_SPECULATIVE_TYPE_NONE} and is only populated by:
  * --spec-type <name>   (common/arg.cpp:4237)
  * a discovered sidecar in the draft repo (common/arg.cpp:559-577)

The draft-model type name is "draft-simple" (common/speculative.cpp:35).

Without --spec-type the server logs "[spec] loading draft model ..." and reserves
the VRAM, but the timings response has no draft_n / draft_n_accepted keys and
throughput is unchanged. That looks like "speculation did not help" but it is
actually "speculation never ran".

Correct invocation:
  llama-server -m <target> -md <draft> -ngld 99 --spec-type draft-simple \
               --spec-draft-n-max 8 ...

